# Independent fixture-path review

Reviewed the uncommitted test_record_smoke.py change on 8778dbc. No blocking finding. The one functional change resolves only the already-created temporary fixture directory before constructing repositories and the site. strict=True rejects missing roots. It does not normalize production payload inputs or weaken real_directory, snapshot, or linked-directory rejection.

The saved macOS CI log has two errors and two failures originating from linked or non-directory ancestor rejection; deadline assertions encountered that earlier exception. Resolving the host temporary root is consistent with existing test_payload fixture setup and macOS /var aliases. The original log remains failure evidence; macOS rerun is required for platform CI confirmation.

Independent Windows test: an actual junction was used as the fixture ancestor. real_directory rejected the original alias; prepare resolved it to its real target; smoke.record then completed with an actual temporary bare Git remote and injected HTTP report. The original junction entry was removed without traversing its target. Existing payload tests all passed, including actual junction rejection and hard-link/output safeguards. No live HTTPS or Pages API was used. The parent separately executes the five smoke tests; those are not claimed as my independent run.
